Example 1 – simplifying
  Simplify &frac{8x}{4}
  Divide numerator and denominator by 4
  8x ÷ 4 = 2x; 4 ÷ 4 = 1
  = 2x
  = 2x
  (Cancel the common factor of 4.)

Example 2 – adding
  Simplify &frac{x}{3} + &frac{x}{4}
  Common denominator = 12
  &frac{4x}{12} + &frac{3x}{12}
  = &frac{7x}{12}
  = &frac{7x}{12}
  (Multiply each fraction to get denominator 12.)

Find a common denominator and add.

(a) &frac{x}{2} + &frac{x}{3}
(b) &frac{x}{4} + &frac{x}{5}
(c) &frac{2x}{3} + &frac{x}{6}
(d) &frac{x}{2} + &frac{3}{4}

Find a common denominator and subtract.

(a) &frac{x}{2} − &frac{x}{5}
(b) &frac{3x}{4} − &frac{x}{3}
(c) &frac{5x}{6} − &frac{x}{2}
(d) &frac{x+1}{3} − &frac{x}{4}

Factorise the numerator or denominator, then cancel.

(a) &frac{x² + 2x}{x}
(b) &frac{3x + 6}{3}
(c) &frac{x² − 4x}{x}
(d) &frac{2x² + 6x}{2x}

